    }
  }
}

[... 8 more lines]
```

The vector has 3 dimensions and the query vector has 2.
The last request is expected to return a `NullPointerException` (500) instead of the row with a warning.
Using a 3-dimensional query vector, such as `[1.0, 0.0, 0.0]`, makes it succeed.

FIELD_EXTRACT throws IllegalArgumentException instead of returning null when a flattened sub-field key is absent from a segment

9.7.0-SNAPSHOT (also observed on a Kibana CI build, same version)

`FIELD_EXTRACT(flattened_field, "path")` is [documented](https://www.elastic.co/docs/reference/query-languages/esql/functions-operators/string-functions/field_extract) to return `null` whenever the requested key doesn't exist for a row:

In practice, this only holds when the key exists somewhere in the index. When a given key is absent either because no document in that segment ever set it, or because `ignore_above` dropped every occurrence of it from indexing, `FIELD_EXTRACT` throws instead of returning `null`:

```
"Line 1:55: evaluation of [FIELD_EXTRACT(data, \"causal_features.feature_id\")] failed, treating result as null. Only first 20 failures recorded."
"Line 1:55: java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: path [causal_features.feature_id] does not exist"
```

```
// 1. Create an index with a flattened field, no ignore_above (pre-migration state)
PUT test_mixed_mapping_era
{
  "mappings": { "properties": { "data": { "type": "flattened" } } }
}

// 2. Index a document under the OLD mapping, refresh (creates its own segment)
POST test_mixed_mapping_era/_doc?refresh=true
{ "data": { "causal_features": [ { "feature_id": "feature-A", "name": "Checkout" } ] } }

[... 13 more lines]
```

A second, even simpler repro doesn't need any mapping migration at all:

```
PUT test_ignore_above_only
{
  "mappings": { "properties": { "attrs": { "type": "flattened", "ignore_above": 10 } } }
}

POST test_ignore_above_only/_doc?refresh=true
{ "attrs": { "long_field": "this-value-is-way-longer-than-ten-characters" } }

POST /_query
{
[... 2 more lines]
```

Found while investigating [elastic/kibana#305278](https://github.com/elastic/kibana/pull/305278), which adds `ignore_above` to an existing `flattened` field (`.rule-events`'s `data` column) via an in-place mapping update on a live, previously-unrestricted data stream.
